# Accounting stable edits (pre-Grok working pattern)

`apps/accounting-sandbox` data lives in the **user’s browser** (`selpic-accounting` IndexedDB on **http://localhost:3001**). Disk code is not the ledger. Storefront `3005` will never show these edits.

## What broke after Grok (19 Aug 2026)

- Incomplete search-replace → `ReferenceError` → accounting **500** / Fast Refresh loop
- Root `npm run clean` used to **kill port 3001**
- `persistRepairedDatesToStatements` wrote speculative US/month+3 folds into IndexedDB, so later code “fixes” never matched the screen
- A mistaken “Q3 $7,570.19 looks wrong” request **folded real Q3 bank into Q4**; the user then said the **pre-change** logic was correct
- **Recover to Statement History** saved the merged cache as `recovered_*.cache` beside the real PDF → doubled History / Q3 32 vs 13

## Pre-Grok pattern (do this)

- Change **display/filter** helpers; do **not** rewrite statement dates or `period` in IndexedDB
- Date repair is **per statement file** only: `repairStatementDateAnomalies` → `repairUsMisparsedAustralianDates`. Never compare one statement against the merged ledger
- `loadAllTransactions` must read **every** saved statement plus all cash expenses. Filtering, skipping, or deleting a History row inside the loader looks exactly like data loss
- Q3 Jan–Mar 2026 = **8 cash + 5 company bank** (13 txs), expenses **$7,570.19**, Bank **$304.38**. That is not Q4 leakage
- Keep both Stamp Zone cash rows (`cash_*` ids)
- `syncLegacyTransactionCache` must never overwrite a non-empty `accounting_transactions` cache with `[]`
- P&L period options must stay selectable at `0 txs`, and every FY the user may pick (ledger FYs + current FY + selected FY) must be listed. A `disabled` empty quarter or a `find(...)` miss that returns without calling `onChangeViewPeriod` reads as "Q4 cannot be selected"
- Surface IndexedDB read failures as an error banner — a silent catch renders “No saved statements found” and reads as deleted data
- The mount effect in `useAccountingDashboard` must call `loadAllTransactions()` / `loadStatementHistory()` **before** its cleanup `return`. A `return` placed mid-effect made every line after it dead code, so the dashboard showed only the small `localStorage` cache and *no* code fix could change the screen (19 Aug 2026 root cause)
- `IDBObjectStore.delete()` resolves even when the key never matched — re-read the record after delete and report failure, otherwise a delete looks ignored
- After a Fast Refresh 500: hard-refresh **3001**, do not Recover unless History is truly empty

## Confirmed fixtures (do not “fix”)

- **ASSOCIATEDCLEANING $3,526.60** on **2026-05-07** and **2026-06-05** — legitimate monthly recurring payment; statement parse is correct. Same amount + description on different dates is **not** a duplicate by itself. Only a **month +3 fold of the same day-of-month** (e.g. 15 Jan → 15 Apr) was corruption from Recover / date heal.
- **ATO GST/BAS refund ~$18** — **not** company income. Increases Cash (asset); P&L Revenue must ignore it. See `.cursor/rules/accounting-ato-gst-refund.mdc`.
- **Nab Intnl Tran Fee** — Bank Fees & Interest expense, but **GST FREE** (no BAS 1B). See `.cursor/rules/accounting-nab-intnl-tran-fee-gst-free.mdc`.

## Do not

- Persist US MM/DD or month±3 folds on every `loadAllTransactions`
- Treat “P&L period 55 vs This statement 50” as a reason to move Q3 bank into Q4
- Add cross-statement date modules (e.g. a `restore-folded-q3-bank-dates` style helper) — deleted 19 Aug 2026 after it moved real rows between quarters
- Compound date heals that fight each other
- Deduplicate or delete rows solely because amount + description match across months (recurring merchants)
- Verify accounting on the homepage port
